<title>FRANCE: Bull down as trading resumes.</title>
<headline>Bull down as trading resumes.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in French computer maker Cie des Machines Bull fell sharply on Friday after trading resumed following the third stage of its privatisation.</p>
<p>At 0834GMT, Bull shares were down 7.91 percent at 46.00 francs in a volume of 9.2 million francs.</p>
<p>Trading in Bull was suspended on April 23. The state sold 17.1 million shares of which some 15 million were sold to institutionals at 38 francs per share and the rest to private investors at 36 francs.</p>
<p>The state now holds a 17 percent stake.</p>
</text>
